<task id="016" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Un-skip /api/office/save contract tests and cover the identity route</title>
    <phase>1 Foundation</phase>
    <gate>012 complete — the identity route must exist before contract coverage can be written for it</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING override row, root CLAUDE.md §8: any task that modifies `tests/**` or carries the `testing` tag runs code-review plus adr-check at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY (binding since 2026-06-26 per ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 spec FR-B07 and ADR-038). This overrides the default STANDARD skip.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified diagnostic work with a named protocol to follow (§F.2 Fixture-Config-FIRST) and named fixture symptoms to investigate. The judgment boundary — fixture defect versus product defect — is handled by an explicit escalation trigger rather than by model tier.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>testing, integration-test, contract-test, bff-api, backend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`POST /api/office/save` — the add-in's entire save spine — has ZERO executing contract coverage: both of its tests are `[Fact(Skip=...)]`, and 13 of 22 tests in the file are skipped. Un-skip the two save tests by FIXING the underlying fixture defects, not by deleting or rewriting the tests away, and add contract coverage for task 012's identity route.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in .NET integration/contract testing with `WebApplicationFactory`, test fixture configuration and auth handlers, and ADR-038's testing strategy. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Both `POST /api/office/save` contract tests (`OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs:48` `Post_OfficeSave_WithValidRequest_Returns202Accepted` and `:82` `Post_OfficeSave_WithoutAuth_Returns401`) execute and pass with their fixture defects fixed at the root; the task 012 identity route has contract coverage including negative and authorization cases; no ADR-038-banned test pattern is introduced; and any real product defect surfaced by un-skipping is filed via `/project-defer-issue-tracking` and escalated rather than fixed in scope.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      plan.md finding **F-f**: `POST /api/office/save` has zero executing contract coverage. Both its tests are `[Fact(Skip)]` at `tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs:48` and `:82`, and 13 of 22 tests in that file are skipped.
      The two skip reasons are specific and are the starting hypotheses, not the conclusions:
      - `:48` — "Requires fully mocked Office services - ContainerId not configured in test"
      - `:82` — "Requires fully mocked Office services - test auth handler always authenticates"
      Both read as FIXTURE problems (a missing config value; an auth handler that cannot represent an unauthenticated caller), which is exactly the class `docs/procedures/test-fixture-contracts.md` and the §F.2 Fixture-Config-FIRST Inspection Protocol exist to handle. The protocol is binding: when a test is skipped suspecting a DI issue, FIRST inspect fixture config, claims and mocks for non-contract values before assuming a DI problem. Root CLAUDE.md §10 records this as one of three binding sub-mechanisms.
      This task also carries task 012's coverage obligation: ADR-038 requires a contract test for every new endpoint, and 012 deliberately defers writing it here so the fixture work happens once.
      Scope discipline: 13 tests are skipped in this file. This task owns the TWO save tests plus the new identity-route coverage. The other 11 are not in scope — record them for a follow-up rather than expanding.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/procedures/test-fixture-contracts.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">The `/api/documents` document-identity resolver route and its request/response contract — the surface this task adds coverage for</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the two save tests at `:48` and `:82`. FIX the underlying fixture defects; do NOT delete the tests, do NOT rewrite them into weaker assertions, and do NOT replace them with a different test that happens to pass. The `Skip` attribute comes off because the cause is gone.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: diagnosis order for every skipped test touched here. Apply the §F.2 Fixture-Config-FIRST Inspection Protocol (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F.2, procedure in `docs/procedures/test-fixture-contracts.md`): FIRST inspect fixture config, claims and mocks for non-contract values, BEFORE assuming a DI-registration problem. Record what you inspected and what you found before making any production-code change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: every test written or modified in this task. Banned patterns: `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` (B1), DI-registration tests (B3), and constructor null-check tests (B4). Also banned: `Stopwatch` plus `Task.Delay` timing tests — use `TimeProvider`. New tests must land at a KEEP path per ADR-038's 7 categories.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this task's boundary. Own the TWO `POST /api/office/save` tests plus new identity-route coverage. The other 11 skipped tests in the file are OUT of scope — record them in notes/ for a follow-up; do not opportunistically un-skip them, and do not let their fixture needs expand this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: findings that are not fixture defects. If un-skipping reveals a REAL PRODUCT DEFECT (the endpoint genuinely misbehaves), file it via `/project-defer-issue-tracking` (writes both `notes/defer-issues.md` and a GitHub Issue) and escalate. Do NOT silently fix product behavior out of scope — that turns a test task into an unreviewed behavior change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: the 401 test at `:82` specifically. The "test auth handler always authenticates" symptom means the fixture cannot represent an unauthenticated caller. Fix that so the endpoint's real `RequireAuthorization()` behavior is exercised — do not assert 401 by bypassing the pipeline or by testing the filter in isolation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: assertions on failure responses. Error shapes are ProblemDetails; assert the contract shape, not an incidental message string.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">Scope: any Dataverse GUID used in test arrangement or assertion. Use canonical bare-lowercase form via the shared helper; do not hand-roll brace stripping in test setup, which would mask a production canonicalization bug.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BFF publish size. If this task touches `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**` at all (for example to fix a fixture-visible config default), measure the publish-size delta against a FRESH BUILD OF MASTER, not the recorded baseline (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). If the task changes only `tests/**`, state that no BFF publish change occurred.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: CI files. Do NOT edit `ci-router.yml`, `ci-tier1-blocking.yml`, or `ci-tier2-advisory.yml` — frozen under the shadow-comparison window opened 2026-08-27.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Contract testing, WebApplicationFactory fixtures, test auth handlers, ADR-038 KEEP paths</topic>
