      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Where authorization actually runs in the pipeline — needed to assert 401/403 against the real pipeline rather than around it.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">The route shape task 012 produced, so the new contract test asserts the real contract.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load project CLAUDE.md, plan.md §3 finding F-f and §6 Testing Strategy, `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md`, `docs/procedures/test-fixture-contracts.md`, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F.2. Declare: RIGOR LEVEL FULL (TEST-MODIFYING override, root CLAUDE.md §8), model-tier sonnet, effort high, steps mode DIRECTIONAL.</step>
    <step order="1">Apply §F.2 Fixture-Config-FIRST to the `:48` skip ("ContainerId not configured in test"). Inspect the fixture's configuration, the claims it issues, and its registered mocks for non-contract values BEFORE touching DI or production code. Write down what you inspected and what you found in notes/ before changing anything.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply §F.2 to the `:82` skip ("test auth handler always authenticates"). The fixture's auth handler apparently cannot represent an unauthenticated caller. Determine how to exercise the real `RequireAuthorization()` path — a client without the test auth scheme, or a fixture variant that can omit authentication — without bypassing the pipeline.</step>
    <step order="3">Fix the fixture defects at their root. Prefer a fixture-side fix; a production-code change is only correct if the fixture was expressing a real contract the product does not honor — and in that case it is a product defect, so fire the escalation trigger instead.</step>
    <step order="4">Remove the two `Skip` attributes and run the tests. `Post_OfficeSave_WithValidRequest_Returns202Accepted` must assert the real 202 contract (success, non-empty JobId, StatusUrl containing `/api/office/jobs/`, StreamUrl containing `/stream`). `Post_OfficeSave_WithoutAuth_Returns401` must assert 401 from the real pipeline.</step>
    <step order="5">Add contract coverage for task 012's identity route: the happy path (a Spaarke-sourced document resolves), the "not a Spaarke document" path (a successful response carrying no identity — NOT a 404 and NOT an error), unauthenticated (401), unauthorized-for-the-resolved-document (403 with no metadata leaked), and malformed input (ProblemDetails 400).</step>
    <step order="6">Verify no banned pattern was introduced: grep the touched test file for `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration assertions, ctor null-check tests, and `Stopwatch`. Confirm new tests sit at an ADR-038 KEEP path.</step>
    <step order="7">Record the remaining 11 skipped tests in the file — id, line, skip reason, and whether the reason looks like a fixture defect or a product gap — in notes/ as a follow-up inventory. Do not un-skip them.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` for the affected test projects. Confirm the two previously-skipped tests now execute and pass and that no previously-passing test regressed.</step>
    <step order="9">If any production code under `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**` was touched, measure publish size against a fresh build of master and record it; otherwise state explicitly that no BFF publish change occurred.</step>
    <step order="10">Update projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="11">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/ — including the full §F.2 diagnosis trail from steps 1 and 2.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If un-skipping reveals a REAL PRODUCT DEFECT rather than a fixture defect — `POST /api/office/save` genuinely returns the wrong status, the wrong shape, or authorizes incorrectly — STOP. File it via `/project-defer-issue-tracking` (both `notes/defer-issues.md` and a GitHub Issue) and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Do NOT silently fix it out of scope; a behavior change smuggled inside a test task bypasses review.</trigger>
    <trigger>If fixing the `:82` fixture requires changing the shared test auth handler in a way that affects other test classes, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — a shared-fixture change has blast radius beyond this file and beyond this project's worktree.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the two save tests cannot be made to execute without introducing a banned pattern (`Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` for the SPE/Graph boundary, for example), STOP and escalate as an ADR-038 tension per CLAUDE.md §6.5 rather than introducing the banned pattern or leaving the test skipped.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the §F.2 inspection shows the skip reason recorded in the attribute is simply wrong (the real cause is different), STOP and record the corrected diagnosis before proceeding — the empirical-reproduction-FIRST protocol (§F.3) applies: hand-trace and reproduce before applying any recommended fix.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test (affected test projects), publish (only if production code was touched)</tool>
    <tool name="git">worktree add for a fresh master publish-size baseline, only if production code was touched</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
