  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs`, when inspecting `Post_OfficeSave_WithValidRequest_Returns202Accepted` (was `:48`), then it has no `Skip` attribute, it executes, and it passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs`, when inspecting `Post_OfficeSave_WithoutAuth_Returns401` (was `:82`), then it has no `Skip` attribute, it executes, and it passes by asserting 401 from the real request pipeline (not by bypassing it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given both tests, when inspected, then neither was deleted, weakened, or replaced — the original assertions (202, non-empty JobId, StatusUrl containing `/api/office/jobs/`, StreamUrl containing `/stream`; and 401) are intact or strengthened.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given notes/, when read, then it records the §F.2 Fixture-Config-FIRST diagnosis trail for BOTH skips — what fixture config, claims and mocks were inspected, and what was found — before any change was made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the task 012 identity route, when the new contract tests run, then the happy path asserts the resolved document identity contract.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a document that is not from Spaarke, when the identity contract test runs, then it asserts a successful response carrying no identity — explicitly NOT a 404 and NOT a ProblemDetails error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unauthenticated caller, when the identity contract test runs, then it asserts 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a caller lacking Read on the resolved document, when the identity contract test runs, then it asserts 403 and asserts that no document metadata appears in the response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a malformed or empty document URL, when the identity contract test runs, then it asserts a ProblemDetails 400 — not a 500 and not an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the touched test file, when grepped, then it contains no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration test, no constructor null-check test, and no `Stopwatch`-based timing assertion (ADR-038 B1/B3/B4).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the file after this task, when the remaining skipped tests are counted, then 11 remain and each is inventoried in notes/ with its line, skip reason, and a fixture-versus-product classification — none was opportunistically un-skipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the full affected test suite, when run, then no previously-passing test regressed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given notes/, when read, then it states either the measured publish-size delta against a fresh master build (if production code was touched) or an explicit statement that only `tests/**` changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `ci-router.yml`, `ci-tier1-blocking.yml`, and `ci-tier2-advisory.yml` are unmodified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    plan.md §3 finding F-f and §6 Testing Strategy. spec.md's testing obligations and ADR-038.
    This task is modify-only over existing test surface (un-skipping and extending tests for endpoints owned by other tasks), so no `justification` block is required per CLAUDE.md §11 ("add tests for existing surface" is modification, not new surface).
    Rigor is FULL by the TEST-MODIFYING override row in root CLAUDE.md §8, not by the default decision tree — the file is under `tests/**` and the tags include `testing`. That override is binding and unconditional.
    `parallel-safe:true`, no wave partner: it depends on task 012 and touches a test file no other Phase 1 task writes to. Task 014 also appends to this file for its own coverage — if 014 and 016 run near each other, 016 should land first or the two must coordinate on that single file.
  </notes>

